1
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:02,740
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,657
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:07,297
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,556
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,035
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,500
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:16,720
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,100
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:24,297
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,477
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,680
This is a time known as
the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:35,300
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:40,540
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,760
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:52,617
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,357
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:58,557
Raise the sails and take the helm.

18
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:01,197
That legendary place.

19
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,877
That the end of the map reveals.

20
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,837
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:10,177
Until someone proves it real.

22
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:12,657
Through it all.

23
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,517
Through all the trouble of times.

24
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,877
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

25
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,617
Know that I will be there.

26
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,357
To stand by you.

27
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:24,280
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

28
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:28,297
So come aboard and bring along.

29
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:30,600
All your hopes and dreams.

30
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,937
Together we will find everything.

31
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:36,080
That we're looking for.

32
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:39,737
There's always room for you.

33
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,500
If you wanna be my friend.

34
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:46,940
We are, we are on a cruise.

35
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,780
We are.

36
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,960
You've raised your prices again?

37
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,760
That's a little steep, don't you think?

38
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:08,200
Raise your prices again
and I'll stop paying.

39
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,820
What's the big deal?

40
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:16,156
It's just one paper.

41
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:17,397
Just one paper?

42
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,617
I buy these every day.

43
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:19,680
Yeah,

44
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,817
but there's no need to
save every last berry

45
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:24,057
so you can buy back your
village from Arlong,

46
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:24,970
you know?

47
00:02:25,053 --> 00:02:27,169
You can finally stop
obsessing about money.

48
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,420
You're so stupid.

49
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:32,580
Now that all that stuff's over,
I'm saving money for me now.

50
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:38,537
Jeez, I'm not gonna be one of those poor
pirates who can't even afford to dress up.

51
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:39,900
Whoa, calm down.

52
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:43,534
I'm in the middle of developing
my special Tabasco star.

53
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:49,048
An eye full of this
will make any bad guy...

54
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,460
Oh, come on!

55
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,012
I just want one of them!

56
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,590
No!

57
00:02:58,673 --> 00:03:00,460
This is Nami's tangerine orchard!

58
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:02,940
I won't let anyone lay a finger on it!

59
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:06,977
Nami, can you see how well
I'm protecting your trees?

60
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,917
Yes, you're doing very well.

61
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,380
Oh, Sanji's getting
used, that poor bastard.

62
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:17,000
I only want one tangerine.

63
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,160
Just give it here.

64
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:20,302
You're so mean.

65
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:21,850
No!

66
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:24,220
Oh, well.

67
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:25,912
I'm pretty happy anyway.

68
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:30,820
The world's sure a turbulent place.

69
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,138
They just had another coup in Villa.

70
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:36,640
What's that?

71
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:41,420
Huh?

72
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:43,000
Ah! Ah!

73
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:44,380
Uh! Huh?

74
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,030
Ah!

75
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:09,990
So,

76
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:12,697
even a conservative
estimate of their power

77
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:15,662
says they're too much for
our branches to handle?

78
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:16,950
That's right.

79
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:18,617
Even before forming his pirate group,

80
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:21,277
he defeated Marine Branch
Captain Axe Hand Morgan,

81
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,066
which he did single-handedly.

82
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:26,358
And since then, he's showed
no signs of slowing down.

83
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,600
Buggy the Clown, 15 million.

84
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:33,100
Pirate Fleet Commodore
Don Krieg, 17 million.

85
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:36,128
Fishman Pirate Sawtooth,
Arlong, 20 million.

86
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:41,377
These pirates were big players, and they
had bounties of over 10 million berries.

87
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:45,320
By comparison, the average
bounty is only 3 million berries.

88
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,059
He took them down.

89
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:53,100
It's true that 30 million berries as a
starting bounty is globally unprecedented.

90
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,700
But in my opinion, it's necessary.

91
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:59,320
It's best to destroy such
seeds of villainy early on,

92
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,325
before they've had a
chance to get out of hand.

93
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:04,370
Absolutely.

94
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,760
All right, guys, we're wanted criminals!

95
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,120
That's a whole lot of fairies!

96
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:14,910
Check it out!

97
00:05:14,993 --> 00:05:16,737
I'll be seen all around the world!

98
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,457
These girls might even fall for you!

99
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:19,370
What?

100
00:05:19,453 --> 00:05:21,160
They put Long Nose in but left me out?

101
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:23,917
Where are you?

102
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,457
I don't see you anywhere.

103
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:26,540
You're not there.

104
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,328
It's the back of your head.

105
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,657
That's not so great.

106
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:33,500
Aw, don't be so glum.

107
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,857
You don't have to be a captain to get
your picture on one of these things.

108
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,180
Huh? Is that true?

109
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,600
Yeah, just work really hard.

110
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:45,520
Let's go to the Grand Line, men!

111
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:50,980
Yet again, you guys don't understand
how grim our situation really is.

112
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:54,535
This means all of our lives
will be in constant danger.

113
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:59,920
Okay, this is no time to be
relaxing in the East Blue.

114
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:05,057
30 million berries.

115
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:08,237
At that amount, I bet
headquarters will take action!

116
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:11,555
Not to mention there'll be
bounty hunters to deal with.

117
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:15,100
And with this kind of
bounty, they'll be good.

118
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:20,690
Miss?

119
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:25,820
Miss Kaya!

120
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:28,120
Miss, it's amazing!

121
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,740
Mary, what's wrong?

122
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,620
Have you seen this, flyer?

123
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,460
Look, it's Usopp!

124
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:38,800
See, that's definitely
Usopp facing the other way!

125
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,880
Hey, you know what?

126
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,140
You're right.

127
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:49,170
Finally!

128
00:06:49,253 --> 00:06:52,100
Luffy, you're finally living your dream!

129
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:54,760
I'm Monkey D.

130
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:57,468
Luffy, and I'm gonna
be king of the pirates!

131
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,420
See ya!

132
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:08,660
But if we meet again,
we will meet as enemies.

133
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,400
We're getting closer.

134
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:47,054
We've almost made it to the Grand Line.

135
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:50,860
There's a famous city on this
island known as Loguetown.

136
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:52,730
Loguetown?

137
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,713
I'm pretty sure I've heard of it before.

138
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,849
It's the city of the
beginning and the end.

139
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:03,409
It's the town where the old
King of the Pirates, Gold Roger,

140
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,600
was both born and killed.

141
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,671
That's where the King of the Pirates died.

142
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:14,450
Well?

143
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:16,660
Yeah, let's do it.

144
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,280
This was the man who had the One Piece.

145
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:24,900
Everything the world has to offer, I need
to see where he was born and executed.

146
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:40,000
If you wish to flee, then do so now.

147
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:45,240
We owe the passion of peace in this
world, and weakness will not be tolerated.

148
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:48,680
The feeble public counts on us.

149
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,900
We alone are the righteous ones.

150
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:54,560
If there is evil on the
seas, then we, the Marines,

151
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:57,707
must drive it away with
the utmost prejudice.

152
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:01,540
In the name of absolute peace!

153
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:04,400
Yes, sir!

154
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:09,057
Woo-hoo!

155
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,800
This is going to be so fun!

156
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:15,580
Every pirate headed to the Grand
Line stops here to resupply.

157
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:18,331
It has everything you could possibly need.

158
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:21,797
If that's the case, then I'm
going to go on a shopping spree.

159
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:24,257
I'll bet they have all
sorts of stuff here.

160
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:26,811
I'll be able to stock up on fresh produce.

161
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,680
And fresh women.

162
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,057
You'd think there'd be a
swordsmith around here.

163
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:32,611
I thought you were broke.

164
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:34,780
Are you going to steal a sword?

165
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:38,337
Well, I'm going to find
out where they kill people.

166
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:39,250
Huh?

167
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:42,617
I've got to see where the King
of the Pirates was executed.

168
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:43,530
Hey, wait!

169
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,760
We have to pick a meeting place!

170
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:48,580
Oh, that's not good.

171
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:54,857
The King of the Pirates was
born and executed in this town.

172
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:59,240
I could be running in his very
footsteps right now. Yahoo!

173
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:04,080
These swords are all
so freaking expensive.

174
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,860
Sure, I'll lend you some money.

175
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:09,760
That'll just be 300 % interest.

176
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:14,337
I can't afford to borrow any
more money from that girl.

177
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:17,757
But I can't go to the grand
line stuck with just one sword.

178
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:19,252
There's got to be a way.

179
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:20,660
Monster, how rude.

180
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,057
Shut up.

181
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:25,417
Our boss is behind bars
because of you and your

182
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:28,500
idiot of a captain Haven't
you learned your lesson?

183
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:29,737
Definitely not.

184
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:31,777
Guess we need you to teach us again!

185
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:33,897
We're supposed to bring your corpse to our

186
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:36,237
boss so he can see that
we finished you off.

187
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:38,997
If you insist, I will fight you!

188
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:41,257
She's really very funny.

189
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:43,640
You do know you're a girl, right?

190
00:11:03,180 --> 00:11:07,620
Oh, she did it that was awesome

191
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:16,299
She's good with a sword,
but not so good at walking.

192
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:18,040
Oh, man.

193
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:19,777
Where are they?

194
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,020
Hey, here you go.

195
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,350
Thanks.

196
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:25,300
That's so kind.

197
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:28,560
May I have my glasses?

198
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,460
How do I look?

199
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:34,717
You look absolutely engaging. And now...

200
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:37,340
Artistically extravagant. This?

201
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:42,460
Considuously elevated, acrimoniously
alteraged, artificially executed,

202
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:45,036
may I deliver these to your lodgings?

203
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:48,780
No thanks, a little too
expensive for my taste.

204
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:50,660
Thank you, come back soon!

205
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,380
Ah, a perfect aperitif.

206
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:56,900
Coupled with two
mouth-watering delicacies?

207
00:11:57,660 --> 00:12:01,260
Oh, with so much on the menu,
I can't decide where to start.

208
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:04,300
Oh, I wish this was a buffet.

209
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:08,740
Whoa, I think I just
found the main course!

210
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,300
Whoa, crazy!

211
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,567
I think I've died and
gone to trinket heaven!

212
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:18,660
Come in, come in!

213
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,377
In our humble store,
almost everything you see?

214
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,177
Is a near priceless pirate artifact.

215
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,197
from Adventure to the Grand Line.

216
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:28,497
I am certain you will not find a
store like this in the entire world.

217
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:31,537
So then, everything in this store
has been to the Grand Line and back?

218
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:32,617
Is that what you're telling me?

219
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:34,300
You are so observant.

220
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:38,337
We only accept a certain type of clientele
in this establishment, you might imagine.

221
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:42,420
And I can tell by your demeanor
that you're my type of client.

222
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:43,870
Observe!

223
00:12:43,953 --> 00:12:45,357
I hold in my hands a gun that was once the

224
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:48,680
favorite of none other than
THE Gold Roger! No way!

225
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:51,100
Gold Roger's gun? Yes.

226
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:53,540
Just breathe, sir.

227
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:54,697
There's more to come.

228
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:57,320
Show me everything! Right this way!

229
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:04,537
Wait hold on excuse me
where are we going i

230
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:07,326
still can't believe that
you broke my glasses.

231
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:12,677
I told you i'll pay you
back okay jeez you'll pay

232
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:15,157
me back you don't look
like you have any money.

233
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:19,497
Am i right well that's
true i am kind of broke

234
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,877
i knew it i can tell by
the look on your face.

235
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,257
that you're pretty desperate.

236
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,170
What is it?

237
00:13:25,253 --> 00:13:26,797
Your sick mother needs medicine?

238
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,017
Or did your wife run
away with another man?

239
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:30,057
And leave you all alone?

240
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:31,917
to raise the children by yourself?

241
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,160
Hey, hold on.

242
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,220
Don't explain.

243
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,820
Just come with me.

244
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:42,990
Marines.

245
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,030
Here.

246
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,277
Once you start working for the
Marines, you'll never have to worry?

247
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:51,177
about money problems ever again.

248
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:52,477
Not a chance in hell.

249
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:54,260
I don't work for Marines.

250
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,716
You can't leave now!

251
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:58,293
I expect to be paid back for my glasses.

252
00:13:58,940 --> 00:13:59,770
Ah, crap.

253
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,874
Sergeant Major, it's time for training.

254
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:04,800
I'll be back to check on you.

255
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:06,620
She's a sergeant?

256
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:12,088
Crap, this is gonna
take the whole damn day!

257
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,030
Unless...

258
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:18,820
Three mop technique work like a charm.

259
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:23,780
One more time!

260
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:31,540
Hey, you!

261
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:33,117
Just what do you think you're doing?

262
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,030
Huh?

263
